# Regina REXX for tests

REXX stages prefer a user-installed **Regina** library and otherwise fall back to the embedded subset interpreter. That fallback hid a real-Regina bug (OUTPUT remainder trim) on machines without Regina.

When running tests (especially `cargo test` / `cargo +stable test --workspace`):

1. Regina must be installed so `libregina.so` / `libregina.so.3` (Linux), `libregina.dylib` (macOS), or `regina.dll` (Windows) is discoverable. Cloud agent VMs: `.cursor/environment.json` `install` installs Ubuntu packages `regina-rexx` and `libregina3-dev`.
2. **Export `PIPE_REQUIRE_REGINA=1`** before `cargo test`. Tests then fail if Regina is not discovered/loaded, instead of silently using the subset interpreter.
3. Do not weaken pipefix or REXX expectations to match the subset interpreter.

`environment.json` has no env-var field (see the current [schema](https://cursor.com/schemas/environment.schema.json)); export the variable in the shell. Contributors without Regina should leave it unset so the suite still passes on the subset path.

Install notes: [README](../../README.md) and [docs/architecture.md](../../docs/architecture.md).
